cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AnthroSim in research, cite the released software version and preserve the exact source revision used for the experiment."
title: "AnthroSim"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Datengu"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-08-22
repository-code: "https://github.com/Datengu/anthrosim"
url: "https://github.com/Datengu/anthrosim"
license: "Apache-2.0"
keywords:
  - agent-based simulation
  - anthropology
  - archaeology
  - reproducibility
  - demography
  - migration
abstract: >-
  AnthroSim is a reproducible agent-based simulation framework for exploring
  human demography, migration, kinship, cultural transmission, and long-run
  social emergence. Version 0.1 establishes a deterministic synthetic
  population-simulation and experiment baseline and is not an empirically
  validated model of human prehistory.
